    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0001324 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0001324">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0011804"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Azalmış kas kuvveti</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="cs">Snížená svalová síla</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Reduced strength of muscles.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>HP:0002309</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>HP:0008979</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>HP:0009012</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>HP:0009061</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMEDCT_US:26544005</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C0151786</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="fr">Asthénie</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="fr">Faiblesse</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="fr">Faiblesse|faiblesse musculaire sévère|faiblasse musculaire et atrophie</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="tr">Kas güçsüzlüğü</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="nl">Muscular weakness</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="cs">Slabost svalů</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="fr">faiblesse musculaire</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="fr">faiblesse musculaire sévère</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Muscle weakness</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Muscular weakness</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0001324</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>It is important clinical to distinguish between muscle weakness, fatigue, and asthenia. Fatigue describes the inability to continue performing a task after multiple repetitions; in contrast, a patient with primary weakness is unable to perform the first repetition of the task. Asthenia is a sense of weariness or exhaustion in the absence of muscle weakness. Conditions that result in intrinsic muscle weakness can be divided into several main categories: infectious, neurologic, endocrine, inflammatory, rheumatologic, genetic, metabolic, electrolyte-induced, or drug-induced.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="es">Debilidad muscular</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="it">Debolezza muscolare</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">Faiblesse musculaire</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Kas güçsüzlüğü</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Muskelschwäche</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="nl">Spierzwakte</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="cs">Svalová slabost</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="ja">筋虚弱</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">肌无力</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label>Muscle weakness</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
