    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0003805 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0003805">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0004303"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="cs">Přítomnost abnormálních vakuol (membránové organely) v sarkolemě. Při histologickém barvení hematoxylinem a eosinem jsou lemované vakuoly čiré vakuoly podobné popcornu s výrazně modrým okrajem. Vakuoly jsou často spojeny s cytoplazmatickými a příležitostně intranukleárními eozinofilními inkluzemi.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Sarcolemma&apos;da anormal vakuollerin (membrana bağlı organellerin) varlığı. Hematoksilen ve eozin ile histolojik olarak boyanmış vakuoller yoğun mavi bir jant ile patlamış mısır benzeri berrak vakuollerdir. Vakuoller genellikle sitoplazmik ve bazen intranükleer eozinofilik inklüzyonlarla alakalıdır</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Presence of abnormal vacuoles (membrane-bound organelles) in the sarcolemma. On histological staining with hematoxylin and eosin, rimmed vacuoles are popcorn-like clear vacuoles with a densely blue rim. The vacuoles are often associated with cytoplasmic and occasionally intranuclear eosinophilic inclusions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>HP:0009029</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C1853932</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="cs">&quot;Rimmed&quot; vakuoly v biopsii</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="tr">Biyopside &apos;çerçeveli koful&apos;</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="tr">Biyopside &apos;çerçeveli&apos; kofullar</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="nl">Rimmed vacuoles on biopsy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="fr">rimmed vacuoles&apos; on biopsy|&apos;rimmed&apos; vacuoles on biopsy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Rimmed vacuoles on biopsy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0003805</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Rimmed vacuoles are characteristic for inclusion-bosy myositis, but are also seen an a number of other diseases. This term implies that rimmed vacuoles are found histologically. In some cases, the majority of muscle fibers are involved, but in others, rimmed vacuoles can be found in only a minority of fibers.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Gerandete Vakuolen</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="nl">Omrande vacuolen</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="es">Vacuolas festoneadas</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">Vacuoles ourlées</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="it">Vacuoli cerchiati</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt">Vacúolos marginados</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="cs">Vakuoly v cytoplazmě</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Çıkıntılanmış vakuoller</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="ja">縁取り空胞</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">镶边空泡</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label>Rimmed vacuoles</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0003805"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="cs">Přítomnost abnormálních vakuol (membránové organely) v sarkolemě. Při histologickém barvení hematoxylinem a eosinem jsou lemované vakuoly čiré vakuoly podobné popcornu s výrazně modrým okrajem. Vakuoly jsou často spojeny s cytoplazmatickými a příležitostně intranukleárními eozinofilními inkluzemi.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <babelon:source_language>en</babelon:source_language>
        <babelon:source_value>Presence of abnormal vacuoles (membrane-bound organelles) in the sarcolemma. On histological staining with hematoxylin and eosin, rimmed vacuoles are popcorn-like clear vacuoles with a densely blue rim. The vacuoles are often associated with cytoplasmic and occasionally intranuclear eosinophilic inclusions.</babelon:source_value>
        <babelon:translation_language>cs</babelon:translation_language>
        <babelon:translation_status>OFFICIAL</babelon:translation_status>
    </owl:Axiom>
