    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0012823">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="tr">Bu altontoloji, fenotipik anomallik altontolojisinde tanımlanan fenotipik anomallikleri, şiddeti, yanallık, başlangıç ​​yaşı ve diğer yönleriyle karakterize etme ve belirtme koşullarını sağlamak üzere tasarlanmıştır</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="cs">Tato subontologie je navržena tak, aby poskytovala termíny pro charakterizaci a specifikaci fenotypových abnormalit definovaných v subontologii Fenotypové abnormality s ohledem na závažnost, lateralitu, věk nástupu a další aspekty.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This subontology is designed to provide terms to characterize and specify the phenotypic abnormalities defined in the Phenotypic abnormality subontology, with respect to severity, laterality, age of onset, and other aspects.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199"/>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2014-06-06T06:34:24Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>HP:0000004</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C4021064</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="tr">Fenotipik modifiye edici</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="cs">Fenotypový modifikátor</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="fr">Phenotypic modifier</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="nl">Phenotypic modifier</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Phenotypic modifier</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0012823</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Note that some of the terms, such as Intellectual disability, have children terms such as Severe intellectual disability that represent precomposed combinations of modifiers and phenotypic abnormality terms. This done where the medical community commonly uses these terms with a fixed meaning (for instance, the Intellectual disability terms are used with specific IQ ranges). For computational reasoning, the semantics are intended to be the same as if there was a combination of the phenotype term and the clinical modifier term.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="cs">Klinický modifikátor</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="tr">Klinik düzenleyici</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="nl">Klinische modifier</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="es">Modificador clínico</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">Modificateur clinique</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">临床调节因素</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label>Clinical modifier</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
