    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0033667 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0033667">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0033665"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="cs">Snížení subjektivního pocitu duševní pohody.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A reduction in the subjective feeling of mental well being.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-02-28T14:50:58Z</dc:date>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="nl">Mental impairment</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="tr">Mental impairment</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="cs">Mentální porucha</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="nl">Reduced mental health</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="tr">Reduced mental health</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="cs">Snížené duševní zdraví</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Mental impairment</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Reduced mental health</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>The WHO defines mental health as a state of well-being in which the individual realizes his or her own abilities, can cope with the normal stresses of life, can work productively and fruitfully, and is able to make a contribution to his or her community. Thus, mental health is not a state of absence of mental illness. Mental health has been defined on the basis of three components of mental health: emotional well-being, psychological well-being and social well-being. Alternatively, mental health can be defined as a dynamic state of internal equilibrium which enables individuals to use their abilities in harmony with universal values of society. Attempts to measure mental health in as objective a fashion as possible may involve questionnaires such as the 36-item Short Form (SF-36) health survey questionnaire. Impaired mental health is characterized by a reduction in the mental component score (MCS).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="es">Salud mental disminuida</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="cs">Zhoršení duševního zdraví</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">心理健康下降</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="ja">精神的健康の低下</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label>Diminished mental health</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
